.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a given pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function reads the file stream pointed to by
.I fp
line by line, searching for occurrences of the substring
.I search_str .
Each matching line is dynamically allocated and stored in the array pointed to by
.I matches .
The caller is responsible for freeing each matched line, as well as the array itself, after use.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.B mygrep()
function returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Kanwar Albir Zulfiqar.
